This chapter shares only pack, Stock, inventory, catalogue, examine and available feature.

Use the page library.
Use the foundation, battle, party, maps, lettering, sound and town map chapters.

A pack has a potions (number), a cursor (number), a notice (text), a save request (number), an antidotes (number), a balls (number), a moon stones (number), a hp ups (number), a found (list of text) and a shop item (number).
There is a pack called Stock whose potions is 0 and whose cursor is 0 and whose notice is "" and whose save request is 0 and whose antidotes is 0 and whose balls is 0 and whose moon stones is 0 and whose hp ups is 0 and whose shop item is 0.

The field finds are place and found message, in that order:
  "Potion" has "Viridian Forest" and "Found a POTION!".
  "Antidote" has "Viridian Forest" and "Found an ANTIDOTE!".
  "Poke Ball" has "Viridian Forest" and "Found a POKE BALL!".
  "Moon Stone" has "Route 2" and "Found a MOON STONE!".
  "HP Up" has "Route 2" and "Found an HP UP!".

To collect an item (text) into a pack:
  Add the item to the pack's found.
  Depending on the item:
    For "Potion":
      Add 1 to the pack's potions.
    For "Antidote":
      Add 1 to the pack's antidotes.
    For "Poke Ball":
      Add 1 to the pack's balls.
    For "Moon Stone":
      Add 1 to the pack's moon stones.
    For "HP Up":
      Add 1 to the pack's hp ups.

To work out the available feature (text) at a column (number) by a map row (number):
  Let the item be the feature at the column by the map row.
  Let the discovery be the field finds for the item.
  If the discovery is not nothing and Journey's place is the discovery's place and the item is in Stock's found:
    The answer is "".
  The answer is the item.

Let the pokemon entry be 0.
Let the item entry be 1.
Let the trainer entry be 2.
Let the save entry be 3.
Let the last field entry be 4.

Let the shop goods be a list of "POTION", "POKE BALL" and "ANTIDOTE".
Let the last shop good be (the number of items in the shop goods) - 1.

The shop prices are price, in that order:
  "POTION" has 300.
  "POKE BALL" has 200.
  "ANTIDOTE" has 100.

The field signs are wording, in that order:
  "TEXT_REDSHOUSE1F_TV" has "There's a movie on TV. Four boys are walking on railroad tracks.".
  "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_OAKSLAB_SIGN" has "OAK POKEMON RESEARCH LAB".
  "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_SIGN" has "PALLET TOWN: Shades of your journey await!".
  "TEXT_ROUTE1_SIGN" has "ROUTE 1: PALLET TOWN - VIRIDIAN CITY".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_SIGN" has "VIRIDIAN CITY: The eternally green paradise".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_MART_SIGN" has "POKE MART: Shop for useful items.".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_MART_SIGN" has "POKE MART: Shop for useful items.".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_POKECENTER_SIGN" has "POKEMON CENTER: Heal your POKEMON!".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_POKECENTER_SIGN" has "POKEMON CENTER: Heal your POKEMON!".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANCITY_GYM_SIGN" has "VIRIDIAN CITY POKEMON GYM".
  "TEXT_ROUTE2_SIGN" has "ROUTE 2: VIRIDIAN CITY - PEWTER CITY".
  "TEXT_ROUTE2_DIGLETTS_CAVE_SIGN" has "DIGLETT'S CAVE".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANFOREST_USE_ANTIDOTE_SIGN" has "If a POKEMON is poisoned, use an ANTIDOTE!".
  "TEXT_VIRIDIANFOREST_LEAVING_SIGN" has "Leaving VIRIDIAN FOREST. PEWTER CITY ahead.".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_SIGN" has "PEWTER CITY: A stone gray city".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_MUSEUM_SIGN" has "PEWTER MUSEUM OF SCIENCE".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_GYM_SIGN" has "PEWTER CITY POKEMON GYM: LEADER BROCK".
  "TEXT_PEWTERCITY_POLICE_NOTICE_SIGN" has "NOTICE: Report suspicious activity to the police.".
  "TEXT_ROUTE22_POKEMON_LEAGUE_SIGN" has "POKEMON LEAGUE: Front gate".

To work out the inscription (text) for a sign (text):
  If the sign is "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_PLAYERSHOUSE_SIGN":
    The answer is "{Journey's trainer}'s house".
  If the sign is "TEXT_PALLETTOWN_RIVALSHOUSE_SIGN":
    The answer is "{Journey's rival}'s house".
  Let the notice be the field signs for the sign.
  The answer is the notice's wording or else "TRAINER TIPS: Check your POKEMON and items often!".

To examine:
  Let the item be the available feature at the column ahead by the row ahead.
  If the item is "":
    Stop.
  Set Journey's mode to dialogue.
  Let the discovery be the field finds for the item.
  If the discovery is nothing:
    Set Journey's message to the inscription for the item.
    Stop.
  Collect the item into Stock.
  Sound "item".
  Set Journey's message to the discovery's found message.

To treat a fighter with a pack:
  If the pack's potions is less than 1:
    Set the pack's notice to "NO POTIONS".
  Otherwise if the fighter's species is "":
    Set the pack's notice to "NO POKEMON".
  Otherwise if the fighter's health is less than 1:
    Set the pack's notice to "CANNOT USE".
  Otherwise if the fighter's health is at least the fighter's maximum health:
    Set the pack's notice to "HP IS FULL".
  Otherwise:
    Set the fighter's health to the smaller of the fighter's maximum health and (the fighter's health + 20).
    Subtract 1 from the pack's potions.
    Set the pack's notice to "HP RESTORED".
    If Journey's mode is battle bag:
      Set Journey's mode to battle.
      Now Score is not cued.
      Respond.
      If Score is not cued:
        Sound "heal".
    Otherwise:
      Sound "heal".

To cure a fighter with a pack:
  If the pack's antidotes is less than 1:
    Set the pack's notice to "NO ANTIDOTES".
  Otherwise if the fighter's status is not "poisoned":
    Set the pack's notice to "NO POISON TO CURE".
  Otherwise:
    Set the fighter's status to "".
    Subtract 1 from the pack's antidotes.
    Set the pack's notice to "POISON CURED".
    Sound "heal".
    If Journey's mode is battle bag:
      Set Journey's mode to battle.
      Respond.

To toss with a pack:
  If the pack's balls is less than 1:
    Set the pack's notice to "NO POKE BALLS".
  Otherwise if Journey's mode is not battle bag:
    Set the pack's notice to "USE IN BATTLE".
  Otherwise:
    Capture.
    If Team's result is "caught" or Team's result is "escaped":
      Subtract 1 from the pack's balls.
      Set Journey's mode to battle.
      If Team's result is "escaped":
        Respond.
    Otherwise:
      If Team's result is "full":
        Set the pack's notice to "PARTY IS FULL".
      Otherwise:
        Set the pack's notice to "TRAINER'S POKEMON".

To check an adventure with a pack:
  If the adventure's parcel is 1:
    Set the pack's notice to "OAK'S PARCEL".
  Otherwise if the adventure's tm34 is 1:
    Set the pack's notice to "TM34 BIDE".
  Otherwise:
    Set the pack's notice to "NO KEY ITEM".

To map a place (text) with a pack:
  If Journey's mode is battle bag:
    Set the pack's notice to "NOT IN BATTLE".
  Otherwise:
    Set Journey's mode to town map.
    Set Journey's selection to the town pin for the place.
    Set the pack's notice to "".

To unpack a pack:
  If the pack's cursor is 0:
    Treat Combat's ally with the pack.
  Otherwise if the pack's cursor is 1:
    Toss with the pack.
  Otherwise if the pack's cursor is 2:
    Cure Combat's ally with the pack.
  Otherwise if the pack's cursor is 3:
    Set the pack's notice to "MOON STONE".
  Otherwise if the pack's cursor is 4:
    Set the pack's notice to "HP UP".
  Otherwise if the pack's cursor is 5:
    Check Journey with the pack.
  Otherwise if the pack's cursor is 6 and Journey's town map is 1:
    Map Journey's place with the pack.
  Otherwise:
    If Journey's mode is battle bag:
      Set Journey's mode to battle.
    Otherwise:
      Set Journey's mode to field menu.
      Set the pack's cursor to 1.

To pause an adventure for a pack with a key (text):
  If the key is "start":
    Set the adventure's mode to field menu.
    Set the pack's cursor to the pokemon entry.
    Set the pack's notice to "".

To close an adventure for a pack with a key (text):
  If the key is "b" or the key is "a" or the key is "start":
    Set the adventure's mode to field menu.
    Set the pack's cursor to the trainer entry.

To arrange a roster for a pack with a key (text):
  If the key is "b":
    If Journey's mode is battle party:
      Set Journey's mode to battle.
    Otherwise:
      Set Journey's mode to field menu.
    Set the pack's cursor to 0.
    Stop.
  If the key is "up":
    Subtract 1 from the pack's cursor.
    If the pack's cursor is less than 0:
      Set the pack's cursor to the roster's count - 1.
  If the key is "down":
    Add 1 to the pack's cursor.
    If the pack's cursor is at least the roster's count:
      Set the pack's cursor to 0.
  If the key is "a" and the roster's count is more than 0:
    Let the slot be the pack's cursor + 1.
    Let the former be the roster's selected.
    Switch to the slot.
    Set the pack's notice to the roster's notice.
    If Journey's mode is battle party and the roster's selected is not the former:
      Set Journey's mode to battle.
      Respond.

To scroll a pack with a key (text):
  If the key is "b" or the key is "start":
    Set Journey's mode to walk.
    Stop.
  If the key is "up":
    Subtract 1 from the pack's cursor.
    If the pack's cursor is less than the pokemon entry:
      Set the pack's cursor to the last field entry.
  If the key is "down":
    Add 1 to the pack's cursor.
    If the pack's cursor is more than the last field entry:
      Set the pack's cursor to the pokemon entry.
  If the key is "a":
    If the pack's cursor is the pokemon entry:
      Set Journey's mode to party.
      Set the pack's cursor to 0.
      Set the pack's notice to "".
    Otherwise if the pack's cursor is the item entry:
      Set Journey's mode to bag.
      Set the pack's cursor to 0.
      Set the pack's notice to "".
    Otherwise if the pack's cursor is the trainer entry:
      Set Journey's mode to trainer card.
    Otherwise if the pack's cursor is the save entry:
      Add 1 to the pack's save request.
      Set the pack's notice to "SAVE REQUESTED".
    Otherwise:
      Set Journey's mode to walk.

To browse a pack with a key (text):
  If the key is "b":
    If Journey's mode is battle bag:
      Set Journey's mode to battle.
    Otherwise:
      Set Journey's mode to field menu.
      Set the pack's cursor to 1.
    Set the pack's notice to "".
    Stop.
  If the key is "up":
    Subtract 1 from the pack's cursor.
    If the pack's cursor is less than 0:
      Set the pack's cursor to 6.
      If Journey's town map is 1:
        Set the pack's cursor to 7.
  If the key is "down":
    Add 1 to the pack's cursor.
    Let the last item be 6.
    If Journey's town map is 1:
      Set the last item to 7.
    If the pack's cursor is more than the last item:
      Set the pack's cursor to 0.
  If the key is "a":
    Unpack the pack.

To shop a pack with a key (text):
  If the key is "b":
    Set Journey's mode to walk.
    Set the pack's notice to "".
    Stop.
  If the key is "up":
    Subtract 1 from the pack's shop item.
    If the pack's shop item is less than 0:
      Set the pack's shop item to the last shop good.
  If the key is "down":
    Add 1 to the pack's shop item.
    If the pack's shop item is more than the last shop good:
      Set the pack's shop item to 0.
  If the key is "a":
    Let the good be (item (the pack's shop item + 1) of the shop goods) or else "".
    Let the offer be the shop prices for the good.
    Let the price be the offer's price or else 0.
    If Journey's wallet is at least the price:
      Subtract the price from Journey's wallet.
      Depending on the good:
        For "POTION":
          Add 1 to the pack's potions.
        For "POKE BALL":
          Add 1 to the pack's balls.
        For "ANTIDOTE":
          Add 1 to the pack's antidotes.
      Sound "item".
      Set the pack's notice to "ITEM BOUGHT".
    Otherwise:
      Set the pack's notice to "NOT ENOUGH MONEY".

To inventory a key (text):
  Depending on Journey's mode:
    For walk:
      Pause Journey for Stock with the key.
    For trainer card:
      Close Journey for Stock with the key.
    For party or battle party:
      Arrange Team for Stock with the key.
    For field menu:
      Scroll Stock with the key.
    For bag or battle bag:
      Browse Stock with the key.
    For shop:
      Shop Stock with the key.

To catalogue:
  Fill Screen from 0 by 0 with 160 over 144 as 3.
  Fill Screen from 3 by 3 with 154 over 138 as 0.
  Depending on Journey's mode:
    For field menu:
      Inscribe "MENU" at 12 by 10.
      Inscribe "POKEMON" at 25 by 27.
      Inscribe "ITEM" at 25 by 43.
      Inscribe "TRAINER" at 25 by 59.
      Inscribe "SAVE" at 25 by 75.
      Inscribe "EXIT" at 25 by 91.
      Let the y be 27 + Stock's cursor * 16.
      Inscribe ">" at 12 by the y.
      Inscribe Stock's notice at 12 by 119.
    For party or battle party:
      Inscribe "POKEMON" at 12 by 8.
      If Team's count is 0:
        Inscribe "NO POKEMON" at 12 by 28.
      Let the slot be 1.
      For each member in Team's members:
        Let the height be 22 + (the slot - 1) * 14.
        Inscribe "{the member's species} L{the member's level} {the member's health}/{the member's maximum health}" at 22 by the height.
        Add 1 to the slot.
      Let the y be 22 + Stock's cursor * 14.
      Inscribe ">" at 10 by the y.
      Inscribe Stock's notice at 12 by 110.
      Inscribe "A SWITCH B BACK" at 12 by 128.
    For bag or battle bag:
      Inscribe "ITEM" at 12 by 8.
      Inscribe "POTION X{Stock's potions}" at 22 by 19.
      Inscribe "POKE BALL X{Stock's balls}" at 22 by 30.
      Inscribe "ANTIDOTE X{Stock's antidotes}" at 22 by 41.
      Inscribe "MOON STONE X{Stock's moon stones}" at 22 by 52.
      Inscribe "HP UP X{Stock's hp ups}" at 22 by 63.
      If Journey's parcel is 1:
        Inscribe "OAK'S PARCEL" at 22 by 74.
      Otherwise if Journey's tm34 is 1:
        Inscribe "TM34" at 22 by 74.
      Otherwise:
        Inscribe "-" at 22 by 74.
      If Journey's town map is 1:
        Inscribe "TOWN MAP" at 22 by 85.
        Inscribe "CANCEL" at 22 by 96.
      Otherwise:
        Inscribe "CANCEL" at 22 by 85.
      Let the y be 19 + Stock's cursor * 11.
      Inscribe ">" at 10 by the y.
      Inscribe Stock's notice at 10 by 114.
      Inscribe "B BACK" at 10 by 130.
    For trainer card:
      Inscribe "TRAINER CARD" at 12 by 10.
      Inscribe "NAME {Journey's trainer}" at 12 by 32.
      Inscribe "MONEY {Journey's wallet}" at 12 by 49.
      If Journey's badge is 1:
        Inscribe "BOULDERBADGE" at 12 by 70.
      Otherwise:
        Inscribe "NO BADGES" at 12 by 70.
      Inscribe "B BACK" at 12 by 125.
    For shop:
      Inscribe "POKE MART" at 12 by 8.
      Let the position be 0.
      For each good in the shop goods:
        Let the offer be the shop prices for the good.
        Inscribe "{the good} {the offer's price or else 0}" at 22 by (26 + the position * 16).
        Add 1 to the position.
      Let the y be 26 + Stock's shop item * 16.
      Inscribe ">" at 10 by the y.
      Inscribe "MONEY {Journey's wallet}" at 12 by 80.
      Inscribe Stock's notice at 12 by 100.
      Inscribe "A BUY  B EXIT" at 12 by 122.
